  "title": "Nahr al-Kalb monuments",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/monument"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The monuments carved on the cliffs here include three Egyptian hieroglyphic steles,\u00a0six Akkadian monuments, several\u00a0Greek and Roman inscriptions,\u00a0Arabic inscriptions,\u00a0a memorial to Napoleon III's 1860 intervention in Lebanon, and a dedication to the 1943 independence of Lebanon from France.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Over twenty rock reliefs (with accompanying inscriptions) are carved into the limestone cliffs around the estuary of the Nahr al-Kalb river.",
